      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T16:30:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: You could just set `device_connected` to the value of `btif_rc_is_connected_peer(peer-\u003ePeerAddress())` when the flag isn\u0027t set and reduce this logic to `if (!device_connected) { /* ... */ }`.\n\n```\nbool device_connected \u003d false;\nif (IS_FLAG_ENABLED(/* ... */) {\n    // As you have it\n} else {\n    device_connected \u003d btif_rc_is_connected_peer(peer-\u003ePeerAddress());\n}\n\nif (!device_connected) {\n    // log\n    return;\n}\n\n```\n\nI think that will keep the functionality pre-flag and make the logic really readable, i.e. \"if new-avrcp -\u003e use this to get device connection state, else -\u003e use the old thing. if the device isn\u0027t connected -\u003e return\"",
